the moments of truth for Bragdon  aggravations will be the october  european council the migration debate  showed that we may not agree on  everything but we agree on the main goal  which is stemming illegal migration to  Europe we decided to continue our focus  on what unites us and what have already  brought results our eu27 working lunch  today we had a good discussion on brexit  which once again reconfirmed our full  unity  first we reconfirmed that there will be  no withdrawal agreement without a solid  operational and legally binding Irish  backstop and we continue to fully  support initial Barnea in his efforts to  find such a model second we agreed to  have a joint political decoration that  provides as much clarity as possible on  the future relations everybody shares  the view that while there are positive  elements in the checkers proposal the  suggested framework for economic  cooperation will not work not least  because it risks undermining the single  market third we also discussed the  timetable for further negotiations in  October we expect maximum progress and  results in the bracket talks then we  will decide whether conditions are there  to call an extraordinary summit in  November to finalize and formalize the  deal  [Music]
 

